# Base Frame — photo selection manifest
# Lists ONLY the shots we keep, and what each becomes in the guide.
# Format:  SOURCE.HEIC   target.webp      (# comments + blank lines ignored)
# Convert with (macOS):
#   tools/convert-build-photos.sh <staging-dir> docs/assets/build/base-frame/photos.manifest docs/assets/build/base-frame
# Convert with (any OS — needs `pip install pillow pillow-heif`):
#   python3 tools/convert_build_photos.py <staging-dir> docs/assets/build/base-frame/photos.manifest docs/assets/build/base-frame
# That holds every output under the 300 KB target in docs/assets/build/README.md,
# stepping quality down and then shrinking if needed. No flags required.
#
# Source: the "1 - Base Frame Build" Drive folder. The sources are already
# numbered in build order, so the NN prefix here is the SOURCE number — that way
# a photo on the page can be traced straight back to the shot on Drive. Letter
# suffixes (12a/12b/12c) are multiple shots of the same moment; "done" in a
# source name marks a completed-frame shot.

1.jpeg           01-long-rail.webp
2.jpeg           02-cross-rail.webp
3.jpeg           03-motor-in-channel.webp
4.jpeg           04-motor-miter-gear.webp
5.jpeg           05-two-motors-per-rail.webp
6.jpg            06-parts-laid-out.webp
7.jpeg           07-closing-channel.webp
8.jpeg           08-hub-shaft-set.webp
9.jpg            09-corner-joint.webp
10.jpeg          10-two-rails-joined.webp
11.jpeg          11-three-sides.webp
12done.HEIC      12a-completed-table.webp
12done(1).HEIC   12b-completed-low-angle.webp
12done(2).HEIC   12c-completed-three-quarter.webp
13.jpg           13-gear-mesh-detail.webp
14.jpg           14-frame-upright.webp
15.jpg           15-leads-through-rail.webp
16done.jpg       16a-completed-top-down.webp
16done(1).jpg    16b-completed-top-down-alt.webp
